# Git Rules

Never modify unrelated files.

Always analyze repository before changes.

Keep commits small.

Keep commits meaningful.

Never delete code without reason.

Never rename folders unless instructed.

Prefer improving existing architecture.

Always preserve project consistency.

Never introduce breaking changes.

Before implementing:

Analyze

Plan

Implement

Review

Then commit.

Every implementation should be production-ready.

Never create temporary code.

Never create fake implementations.